      "source_excerpt": "Each pigment can absorb different wavelengths of light, which allows the plant to absorb any light that passes through the taller trees. (credit: Jason Hollinger) How Light-Dependent Reactions Work The overall purpose of the light-dependent reactions is to convert light energy into chemical energy.\n…\nThis chemical energy will be used by the Calvin cycle to fuel the assembly of sugar molecules.",
